WEBVTT

01:49.600 --> 01:51.200
LU'S SHOP

02:07.720 --> 02:10.280
LU'S SHOP

02:15.360 --> 02:16.640
You're Mr. Lu, right?

02:17.480 --> 02:18.320
Yes.

02:28.640 --> 02:31.000
This pair of shoes… I've seen them.

02:32.720 --> 02:34.800
Did someone ask you
to make these this summer?

02:34.880 --> 02:36.120
Who was that person?

02:36.800 --> 02:37.640
No idea.

02:38.720 --> 02:40.640
My dad took that job.

02:40.720 --> 02:43.280
He's out of town getting materials.
Maybe in two days?

02:51.560 --> 02:55.040
Two days later,
that young officer showed up on time.

02:55.640 --> 02:56.520
He met my dad.

03:05.920 --> 03:06.760
That's right.

03:07.480 --> 03:10.360
Half a year ago, a young guy came to me.

03:10.440 --> 03:13.560
He insisted I turn
a perfectly good pair of red heels

03:13.640 --> 03:15.360
into blue ones.

03:15.440 --> 03:18.280
It just felt off,
so I didn't want the job.

03:19.280 --> 03:21.680
But then he offered me 800 yuan.

03:21.760 --> 03:23.360
Eight hundred yuan

03:23.440 --> 03:25.800
could buy several pairs
of brand-name shoes.

03:26.360 --> 03:29.240
A real pair of shoes,
he wanted it turned fake.

03:29.320 --> 03:31.480
What was he after?

03:32.480 --> 03:34.480
What did he look like? Do you remember?

03:36.480 --> 03:38.720
A guy in his thirties.

03:38.800 --> 03:39.920
Wearing sunglasses.

03:40.000 --> 03:42.400
His face… I didn't see clearly.

03:43.480 --> 03:44.520
How tall?

03:45.440 --> 03:46.440
His height…

03:47.920 --> 03:49.520
You, stand up.

03:53.040 --> 03:54.160
About my son's height.

03:54.240 --> 03:55.600
Around 175 cm.

03:55.680 --> 03:57.000
Short haircut.

03:57.080 --> 03:58.800
When he spoke, his voice was hoarse.

03:59.440 --> 04:01.520
He had three burn marks on his arm.

04:03.000 --> 04:03.840
Burn marks?

04:03.920 --> 04:05.760
Scars from being burned with cigarettes.

04:12.000 --> 04:14.280
RAN FANGXU'S PATH

04:14.360 --> 04:15.720
BLUE LEATHER HEELS, LILI

04:15.800 --> 04:17.440
DU MINGLIANG'S MOTHER, SHOE SELLER
LIU GUIFANG

04:17.519 --> 04:22.280
SHOEMAKER MR. LU
MAN WITH THREE BURN SCARS

04:22.360 --> 04:26.120
This man is key to solving
the Yuanlongli June 30th case.

04:26.840 --> 04:29.040
Very likely, he's the real killer.

04:30.000 --> 04:31.480
Same plan as always.

04:31.560 --> 04:32.680
We cover both ends.

04:32.760 --> 04:35.120
I'll stay in Yuanlongli.

04:35.200 --> 04:37.720
You go to the branch
and check local stations.

04:37.800 --> 04:40.600
Try to find any useful leads.

04:40.680 --> 04:42.320
This is like finding a needle
in a haystack.

04:42.400 --> 04:45.920
If we had fingerprints,
I could search the database.

04:46.000 --> 04:48.520
But those burn scars,
how do I even ask about that?

04:50.760 --> 04:54.080
I think Uncle Ran went through
the same thing back then.

04:54.680 --> 04:57.480
Otherwise, he would've caught
that guy already.

04:58.800 --> 05:00.720
Just… think it through again.

05:01.400 --> 05:04.600
If you were Uncle Ran,
where would you go next?

05:05.760 --> 05:07.640
RAN FANGXU'S PATH

05:20.280 --> 05:23.120
Han, it's me.

05:23.640 --> 05:24.480
Um…

05:26.680 --> 05:29.040
Hang on! Let me tell you in a second!

05:47.440 --> 05:48.440
My eyes are going blurry.

05:48.520 --> 05:51.720
No idea which idiot came up with this
just to mess with me.

05:55.760 --> 05:56.720
Uncle Ran,

05:57.760 --> 06:00.320
looking at all that stuff,
doesn't it annoy you?

06:00.960 --> 06:01.800
Of course.

06:02.480 --> 06:04.360
It's worse when you can't find clues.

06:05.240 --> 06:09.800
But I have a theory
that helps solve tough problems.

06:09.880 --> 06:10.680
Tell me!

06:15.120 --> 06:17.520
Look, when you're solving a problem,

06:17.600 --> 06:19.120
it's like untangling a ball of thread.

06:19.720 --> 06:21.160
You have to look closely

06:21.800 --> 06:22.840
and find the loose end.

06:24.000 --> 06:27.200
Once you find it, just pull,

06:28.040 --> 06:30.680
and the whole thing unravels.

06:31.720 --> 06:34.200
Right now, I'm looking for that end.

06:38.320 --> 06:40.280
The wind blew it away.

06:40.360 --> 06:42.160
Now it's even harder to find.

06:42.240 --> 06:44.720
That's weird. Why is it so windy today?

06:50.240 --> 06:51.440
Thanks.

07:00.600 --> 07:02.840
PHYSICAL EVIDENCE PHOTOS

07:21.680 --> 07:24.840
LIST OF EVIDENCE

07:26.400 --> 07:29.040
The key to this case… What is it?

07:30.920 --> 07:31.840
‎WHERE DID YOU HIDE THEM?

07:31.920 --> 07:33.000
‎I DIDN'T HIDE THEM. SIR, DID YOU CATCH ME
‎BECAUSE SOMETHING HAPPENED TO MENGMENG?

07:35.520 --> 07:37.480
Why so dumb?

07:40.440 --> 07:41.400
Who are you calling dumb?

07:43.960 --> 07:45.520
Me.

07:45.600 --> 07:47.520
There's been a loose thread here.

07:47.600 --> 07:49.440
How did I miss it?

07:49.520 --> 07:51.000
Q: DID YOU EVER GIFT XU MENG CLOTHING?
A: YES.

07:52.360 --> 07:54.880
Xiaohe, pass me the tape.

08:12.960 --> 08:15.560
PUBLIC SECURITY

08:17.320 --> 08:18.960
WEIYANG PUBLIC SECURITY
BUREAU NANSHAN BRANCH ARCHIVE ROOM

08:27.880 --> 08:29.200
CRIMINAL INVESTIGATION FILES

08:33.480 --> 08:34.679
CRIMINAL INVESTIGATION FILES

08:48.800 --> 08:50.920
Q: DID YOU EVER GIFT XU MENG CLOTHING?
A: YES.

08:56.840 --> 08:58.400
Q: ANY BOWLS DRESS?

08:58.480 --> 09:00.280
A: I MIGHT. I BOUGHT 11 DRESSES
ALL COME WITH DRY CLEANING GIFT CARD

09:00.360 --> 09:03.120
When we interrogated Sun Zhengyong,
I was there too.

09:03.640 --> 09:05.800
Sun Zhengyong had an alibi.

09:05.880 --> 09:08.280
Qu Dahai can also testify for him.

09:08.360 --> 09:10.280
He's not related
to the Yuanlongli June 30th case.

09:11.000 --> 09:14.640
And the Bowls dress
mentioned in the statement,

09:14.720 --> 09:18.120
Xiao Ran already checked the store's
sales records back then.

09:18.200 --> 09:19.520
Everything matched.

09:19.600 --> 09:21.800
Are you sure
this is the loose thread he meant?

09:21.880 --> 09:24.400
I saw Uncle Ran place the tape myself.

09:24.960 --> 09:26.920
Dad, try to think carefully again.

09:27.000 --> 09:29.160
Back then, did Uncle Ran ever mention

09:29.240 --> 09:32.120
the Bowls dress or Sun Zhengyong?

09:45.440 --> 09:46.560
We're back.

09:48.000 --> 09:50.600
BLESSING

09:53.640 --> 09:55.880
You didn't cause Uncle Ran
any trouble, right?

09:55.960 --> 09:57.600
Xiaohe was very well-behaved today.

09:58.120 --> 10:02.040
She even did great
and caught up on all her missed work.

10:02.720 --> 10:04.600
That's all thanks to Uncle Ran.
He taught me well.

10:04.680 --> 10:05.680
Unlike some people,

10:05.760 --> 10:06.920
ask them anything,

10:07.000 --> 10:08.920
they know nothing,
and just shake their head.

10:09.640 --> 10:11.880
Are you taking a jab at me?

10:12.720 --> 10:15.160
I get a question right sometimes, okay?

10:15.240 --> 10:17.120
If teachers taught like Uncle Ran,

10:17.200 --> 10:18.840
using that detective mindset,

10:18.920 --> 10:20.120
I would've graduated early.

10:20.960 --> 10:25.000
You, are you trying to graduate early
to go to Beijing for rock music?

10:25.600 --> 10:27.000
I could even become a cop on the side.

10:28.360 --> 10:30.080
What, on the side?

10:30.160 --> 10:32.480
You, put in the same effort
you use for rock music,

10:32.560 --> 10:35.480
you still wouldn't match
even half of your Uncle Ran's skills.

10:35.560 --> 10:36.960
Uncle Ran isn't a superhero.

10:37.040 --> 10:38.480
He can't even read sheet music.

10:40.360 --> 10:41.480
How about this?

10:41.560 --> 10:43.000
You teach me music notation,

10:43.080 --> 10:44.200
and I teach you criminal investigation.

10:44.280 --> 10:46.040
We learn from each other.

10:46.120 --> 10:47.240
Then who's the teacher?

10:48.120 --> 10:48.960
We both are.

10:50.200 --> 10:51.160
Deal.

10:51.960 --> 10:53.400
Deal.

10:53.480 --> 10:54.400
Rock on.

10:55.200 --> 10:56.040
And even threw up a rock sign?

10:56.120 --> 10:58.840
Hurry and go wash some fruit
for your teacher.

11:05.320 --> 11:07.840
Sir, your package.

11:10.200 --> 11:11.560
QI YUANSHAN

11:13.880 --> 11:15.320
This is the Mount Wu accident file.

11:15.920 --> 11:17.120
We don't need it now.

11:17.200 --> 11:18.160
Perfect timing.

11:18.240 --> 11:20.320
I just wrote something.
Take a look for me.

11:23.920 --> 11:26.160
DEADLY BUILDING CASE
YUANLONGLI JUNE 30TH MEMOIR

11:26.880 --> 11:28.640
This title, it's catchy.

11:29.840 --> 11:32.240
If this gets published,
the title alone will sell it out.

11:33.040 --> 11:35.000
Titles are just for show.

11:35.080 --> 11:36.320
I care more about the content.

11:40.640 --> 11:42.800
ON THE DAY OF JUNE 30TH, 1997…

11:46.080 --> 11:49.400
Times change. Energy's limited.
Focus on the big stuff.

11:50.000 --> 11:51.560
Start with clothes and food.

11:52.080 --> 11:53.920
I get the first three lines.

11:54.000 --> 11:55.920
What does the last one mean?

11:56.000 --> 11:57.200
It's simple.

11:57.880 --> 11:59.400
What can't we live without?

11:59.920 --> 12:01.400
Eating, drinking, and daily needs.

12:01.480 --> 12:03.480
Those things leave clues most easily.

12:05.720 --> 12:06.760
Sir.

12:07.640 --> 12:09.120
That's a great rule.

12:09.200 --> 12:10.520
Why cross it out?

12:11.440 --> 12:13.640
Those were just silly rhymes I made up.

12:13.720 --> 12:14.800
So much for being a top student.

12:14.880 --> 12:17.400
A few words from me fooled you
into calling me "Sir".

12:21.960 --> 12:23.560
Actually, the Yuanlongli June 30th case

12:23.640 --> 12:25.640
has two clothing-related clues.

12:26.560 --> 12:28.120
One is the blue heels.

12:29.720 --> 12:31.360
The other is the Bowls dress.

12:33.360 --> 12:34.200
Right, sir.

12:34.800 --> 12:37.000
Did you write
the Sun Zhengyong interrogation part?

12:38.440 --> 12:39.400
Not yet.

12:39.480 --> 12:40.880
I'm only at Song Qingsong.

12:40.960 --> 12:42.680
Sun Zhengyong, like Song Qingsong,

12:42.760 --> 12:44.480
later ran off
because of illegal fundraising

12:44.560 --> 12:45.560
and debt evasion.

12:46.520 --> 12:49.120
Are you also handling financial cases now?

12:49.200 --> 12:51.520
How did you get to Sun Zhengyong?

12:54.480 --> 12:57.560
Ran did mention Sun Zhengyong to me.

12:58.520 --> 12:59.840
Back then, Uncle Ran

12:59.920 --> 13:01.760
was holding a photo
before he mentioned the loose thread.

13:02.640 --> 13:06.720
But what exactly was in the photo,
I don't know.

13:07.760 --> 13:08.920
A photo.

13:09.800 --> 13:10.920
The loose thread.

13:12.560 --> 13:13.720
Sun Zhengyong.

13:17.880 --> 13:20.360
RAN FANGXU'S PATH

13:20.440 --> 13:23.440
Could it be the dress from Xu Meng's home?

13:24.040 --> 13:25.520
Check it now.

13:25.600 --> 13:28.200
There should be a photo
of a dress in the files.

13:28.280 --> 13:29.840
It's a Bowls dress.

13:30.880 --> 13:32.800
I've gone through
these two boxes a hundred times.

13:32.880 --> 13:34.760
There's no photo of a Bowls dress.

13:35.760 --> 13:37.840
Could it have been borrowed by Uncle Ran,

13:37.920 --> 13:39.640
like those blue heels?

13:40.960 --> 13:43.960
Ran must have compared the photo

13:44.680 --> 13:46.480
and found a problem in the statement.

13:46.560 --> 13:48.760
Go there now. Go to the Bowls store.

13:49.360 --> 13:51.360
Check Sun Zhengyong's purchase records.

13:59.880 --> 14:00.800
Hello.

14:00.880 --> 14:01.960
Hello.

14:02.880 --> 14:04.800
From Nanshan Branch.
I'm here to ask about something.

14:05.320 --> 14:06.720
Ask away, Officer.

14:09.440 --> 14:10.840
You're Jessica too?

14:10.920 --> 14:12.680
When I came five years ago,

14:12.760 --> 14:14.560
there was a male staff member
with the same name.

14:15.320 --> 14:17.240
Here, we change staff, not names.

14:19.360 --> 14:20.480
I wanted to ask.

14:21.440 --> 14:25.520
In 1997, did buying this dress
come with a dry-cleaning card?

14:25.600 --> 14:26.440
Yes.

14:26.520 --> 14:28.440
Not every style did.

14:28.520 --> 14:30.520
But this one is a Bowls classic.

14:30.600 --> 14:32.360
No matter what year you bought it,
it came with one.

14:32.440 --> 14:34.800
And it was a Bowls dry-cleaning card.

14:36.200 --> 14:37.240
Is this it?

14:38.000 --> 14:39.040
That's right. That's the one.

14:39.960 --> 14:43.280
Can you use this card
to find out who bought the dress?

14:44.600 --> 14:45.680
I'm afraid not.

14:45.760 --> 14:47.680
The dry-cleaning cards aren't numbered.

14:50.320 --> 14:51.440
One moment.

14:54.120 --> 14:56.560
This dress was once
brought in for dry cleaning.

14:56.640 --> 14:59.520
Look. Here. There's a check mark.

15:01.400 --> 15:02.320
If it was dry-cleaned,

15:02.400 --> 15:03.880
we can find the record.

15:03.960 --> 15:05.800
I can pull up all the dry-cleaning records

15:05.880 --> 15:08.120
for this dress from 1997.

15:08.200 --> 15:10.120
Dry-cleaning records
are linked to sales records.

15:10.720 --> 15:12.400
-Thank you so much.
-You're welcome.

15:16.120 --> 15:17.200
-Hello.
-Hello.

15:17.280 --> 15:18.520
Excuse me. How can I help you?

15:18.600 --> 15:20.840
I wanted to ask. This store,
how long has it been open?

15:21.880 --> 15:23.600
Our store is the Weiyang flagship store.

15:23.680 --> 15:24.680
It's been open for over 20 years.

15:27.320 --> 15:30.600
Then back in 2003,
did you see this person?

15:30.680 --> 15:31.800
2003?

15:32.320 --> 15:33.440
I was still in high school then.

15:36.960 --> 15:40.520
So, do you have sales records
for the 1997 classic dress?

15:41.160 --> 15:43.200
I'm sorry. Those are internal documents.

15:43.280 --> 15:44.480
We can't just show them.

15:45.520 --> 15:46.760
Police investigation.

15:46.840 --> 15:48.520
It's not that I won't help.

15:48.600 --> 15:51.600
Our store's sales records
are kept for five years at most.

15:52.120 --> 15:54.080
Back in 1997, they were still paper files.

15:54.160 --> 15:55.440
They were destroyed long ago.

15:57.640 --> 15:59.760
But the provincial headquarters
has an archive room.

15:59.840 --> 16:02.080
They should have digital backups.
You can ask there.

16:03.440 --> 16:04.920
Provincial headquarters.

16:05.000 --> 16:06.120
Thank you.

16:07.600 --> 16:09.640
Officer, I'm sorry.

16:09.720 --> 16:11.680
The 1997 records have all been archived.

16:11.760 --> 16:13.120
We need to apply to headquarters.

16:13.200 --> 16:15.120
It'll take about two or three days.

16:17.480 --> 16:18.320
Thanks, that'd be great.

16:18.400 --> 16:19.760
-I'll come back in two days.
-Okay.

16:19.840 --> 16:22.160
HUOFENG INSURANCE

16:44.160 --> 16:45.200
Qiao.

16:51.440 --> 16:53.320
Ran, why did you ask me
to dinner so suddenly?

16:53.400 --> 16:54.440
I wasn't even

16:55.520 --> 16:56.480
prepared.

16:57.520 --> 16:59.080
Why prepare for dinner?

16:59.920 --> 17:00.960
What do you want?

17:02.360 --> 17:03.640
Just some rice noodles is fine.

17:06.680 --> 17:09.000
You ordered braised ribs,
sweet-and-sour fish,

17:09.079 --> 17:12.040
boiled beef, and boiled shrimp,
mushrooms with greens, and egg soup.

17:12.119 --> 17:13.839
Six dishes total.
Would you like anything else?

17:13.920 --> 17:15.400
The shrimp,

17:16.480 --> 17:17.400
maybe skip it.

17:17.480 --> 17:18.520
That's all for now.

17:18.599 --> 17:21.079
-Please serve it quickly.
-Sure.

17:23.240 --> 17:25.800
You ordered too much.
It's expensive and wasteful.

17:26.480 --> 17:28.640
It's fine. We can take leftovers home.

17:37.080 --> 17:38.880
FILE

17:40.200 --> 17:43.920
I pulled this from the evidence room.

17:44.760 --> 17:46.480
After thinking it over,

17:47.960 --> 17:50.000
it's best to leave it with you.

18:00.560 --> 18:02.360
Don't open it yet.

18:04.720 --> 18:07.160
Then, when you tell me to open it,

18:07.240 --> 18:09.320
I'll open it then.

18:16.480 --> 18:17.840
FILE

18:27.760 --> 18:29.000
What's wrong?

18:29.080 --> 18:32.080
On New Year's Eve, what are your plans?

18:32.800 --> 18:34.280
Are you going home?

18:37.840 --> 18:39.640
I don't even have family anymore.

18:39.720 --> 18:41.320
What home is there to go back to?

18:41.400 --> 18:43.480
I'm sorry.

18:46.280 --> 18:48.760
All these years,
I've hated two holidays most.

18:49.960 --> 18:51.520
One is Mid-Autumn Festival,

18:52.360 --> 18:53.800
the other is New Year.

19:07.480 --> 19:08.360
Qiao.

19:11.280 --> 19:12.360
I'm actually

19:13.560 --> 19:18.040
here today to see you
because Sir asked me to.

19:19.920 --> 19:25.200
On New Year's Eve,
he wants to invite you over for dinner.

19:26.680 --> 19:28.400
I'm an outsider. It wouldn't be right.

19:28.480 --> 19:29.720
You guys go ahead and celebrate.

19:31.000 --> 19:32.720
Sir's exact words were,

19:33.240 --> 19:36.680
"Family should have
a reunion dinner together."

19:57.840 --> 19:59.520
If it doesn't work for you,

19:59.600 --> 20:01.080
I I can tell him

20:01.160 --> 20:02.520
-you're going out of town.
-It works for me!

20:05.960 --> 20:06.960
It really is.

20:08.640 --> 20:12.840
But on New Year's Eve,
I promised to take a part-time job.

20:12.920 --> 20:14.200
I might be a little late.

20:14.720 --> 20:16.040
But not too late.

20:16.560 --> 20:19.280
I will come as soon as I'm done.

20:21.960 --> 20:22.840
It's okay.

20:23.800 --> 20:24.920
I'll pick you up then.

20:49.560 --> 20:51.000
BOWLS DRESS

20:56.080 --> 20:56.920
Kiddo,

20:57.880 --> 20:59.920
do you ever get this feeling?

21:00.000 --> 21:04.600
I keep feeling that this Bowls lead,
just like the blue heels,

21:06.000 --> 21:08.080
is a dead end. It goes nowhere.

21:08.160 --> 21:09.000
MAN WITH THREE BURN SCARS

21:10.920 --> 21:13.800
Yuanlongli's demolition is two weeks away.

21:14.400 --> 21:15.720
We need to hurry.

21:15.800 --> 21:18.560
Run the Tremaux algorithm
a few more times.

21:18.640 --> 21:19.640
Again?

21:20.440 --> 21:22.280
You keep running it
on the same few places.

21:22.880 --> 21:23.840
You're just going in circles.

21:24.680 --> 21:26.840
You might as well go to
the provincial capital with me tomorrow.

21:27.440 --> 21:30.400
Whether Bowls is a dead end,
we won't know until we go.

21:34.600 --> 21:36.280
Who messed with this?

21:36.360 --> 21:37.840
Who pulls something like this at night?

21:37.920 --> 21:40.160
Stay away from the window.

21:48.480 --> 21:50.480
Quick, go. Inside, inside.

22:04.760 --> 22:07.120
HOLDOUTS GROUP MESSAGE

22:13.080 --> 22:16.560
Who smashed my window? Was it Qian Dajun?

22:16.640 --> 22:17.480
Get out here!

22:17.560 --> 22:19.200
Is someone going crazy out there?

22:20.480 --> 22:23.560
DU MINGLIANG'S MOTHER
SHOE SELLER, LIU GUIFANG

22:42.920 --> 22:44.680
That Qian Dajun.

22:44.760 --> 22:47.880
Today he smashed a window,
tomorrow he'll break down the door.

22:49.680 --> 22:50.920
I can't go to the provincial capital.

22:51.000 --> 22:52.080
Someone has to stay home.

22:52.680 --> 22:53.760
You go and come back fast tomorrow.

22:54.480 --> 22:56.200
Dad, then promise me.

22:56.280 --> 22:57.760
No matter what happens,

22:57.840 --> 22:59.120
don't get physical.

22:59.200 --> 23:00.560
Call the police if you have to.

23:01.800 --> 23:05.080
With what little they can do,
why would I need the police?

23:06.960 --> 23:08.120
Dad.

23:15.280 --> 23:18.040
Fine. I promise.

23:18.120 --> 23:19.880
If I can argue, I won't fight.

23:20.560 --> 23:21.440
Promise me.

23:23.040 --> 23:24.920
I promise. I promise.

23:28.800 --> 23:31.120
Just don't bother with it today.
Get some sleep.

23:32.040 --> 23:33.920
When I'm back tomorrow, I'll help you.

23:40.160 --> 23:42.360
Be careful going downstairs.

24:00.760 --> 24:02.880
MAN WITH THREE BURN SCARS, BOWLS DRESS

24:02.960 --> 24:04.960
MOTHER OF DU MINGLIANG IN ROOM 1706
SHOEMAKER MR. LU

24:05.040 --> 24:07.320
SONG QINGSONG LIVED IN 1703
OFTEN BROUGHT BACK DIFFERENT GIRLS

24:07.400 --> 24:09.800
RAN FANGXU'S PATH

24:36.040 --> 24:36.880
Hello?

24:36.960 --> 24:39.520
Where are you?
The case briefing is about to start.

24:39.600 --> 24:41.240
-I can't make it back today.
-What?

24:41.320 --> 24:43.160
The case report,
I sent it to Captain Qu last night.

24:43.240 --> 24:45.320
Director Zou wants to praise
you by name at the briefing.

24:45.400 --> 24:48.000
-How can you not be there?
-I'm dealing with something urgent.

24:48.080 --> 24:49.520
I'll ask Captain Zhao
to file my leave request later.

24:50.200 --> 24:51.800
What are you busy with? Why so urgent?

24:54.680 --> 24:55.840
Captain Ran's last wish.

25:26.000 --> 25:27.760
Qiao. Come on.

25:27.840 --> 25:28.760
Have a seat inside.

25:39.720 --> 25:40.560
Uncle He.

25:41.720 --> 25:42.840
I need to apologize to you.

25:44.200 --> 25:47.640
About the demolition,
I did my best to persuade the boss.

25:47.720 --> 25:49.520
But he still sided with Qian Dajun.

25:49.600 --> 25:52.840
He's already given him
full control of the demolition.

25:52.920 --> 25:56.400
Yuanlongli
will likely be demolished early.

25:56.480 --> 25:57.560
I figured.

25:58.080 --> 26:00.040
They started playing dirty last night.

26:05.680 --> 26:06.520
I'm sorry, Uncle He.

26:06.600 --> 26:08.600
Why are you apologizing?

26:08.680 --> 26:09.680
It's not your fault.

26:10.840 --> 26:12.800
It's actually better that you're not
caught in the middle.

26:13.800 --> 26:15.480
Uncle He, please don't do anything rash.

26:15.560 --> 26:18.000
Qian Dajun might do something even worse.

26:18.080 --> 26:19.080
-Who knows what he'll do?
-Let him!

26:19.160 --> 26:20.880
I dare him to try!

26:21.640 --> 26:22.640
Uncle He.

26:22.720 --> 26:24.840
If anything happens to you,

26:24.920 --> 26:27.520
Ran won't be at peace in the afterlife.

26:28.120 --> 26:29.920
To see the Eye of the Vortex,

26:30.440 --> 26:32.800
you must become part
of the Eye of the Vortex.

26:35.360 --> 26:37.040
Those were Ran's words.

26:37.120 --> 26:38.360
None of you understood him.

26:39.480 --> 26:41.320
Only by making up for his regrets

26:41.400 --> 26:43.040
can he find peace.

26:50.440 --> 26:51.280
Uncle He.

26:51.360 --> 26:56.720
Ran gave this to me
just before New Year in 2003.

26:56.800 --> 26:59.960
I don't know
if it can help with what you're doing.

27:01.960 --> 27:03.440
Ran gave you this?

27:03.520 --> 27:04.360
What is it?

27:07.080 --> 27:08.360
I promised Ran

27:08.960 --> 27:10.680
I'd only open it

27:11.920 --> 27:12.960
when he said I could.

27:13.560 --> 27:16.680
But he never got to say it.

27:21.120 --> 27:22.720
SEAL

27:37.680 --> 27:39.360
LIANGLIANG COMPUTER SUPPLIES

27:43.040 --> 27:45.040
What are you doing? Building a bunker?

27:45.120 --> 27:47.920
Uncle He, the surface world has fallen.

27:48.000 --> 27:49.720
Next is our underground world.

27:49.800 --> 27:51.480
I have to arm myself.

27:52.880 --> 27:54.120
Open up and let me in first.

27:54.200 --> 27:55.120
Right.

28:07.960 --> 28:11.120
Uncle He, this drive was formatted.

28:11.200 --> 28:13.560
Everything inside was wiped.
It's all gone.

28:15.760 --> 28:16.680
What do we do?

28:17.240 --> 28:18.400
Can you recover it?

28:18.480 --> 28:20.720
This belonged to Officer Ran.
It's important.

28:21.280 --> 28:22.320
Three minutes.

28:27.520 --> 28:29.040
‎TOOLS, OPEN DISK

28:34.200 --> 28:35.040
Almost done.

28:36.680 --> 28:41.240
BOWLS INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.

28:44.400 --> 28:46.680
You must be Officer He, right?

28:47.240 --> 28:48.480
-Hello.
-Hello.

28:48.560 --> 28:51.840
BOWLS INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.

28:54.160 --> 28:55.200
WEIYANG STORE

28:55.280 --> 28:56.720
1996 to 2005.

28:57.720 --> 28:59.880
The Weiyang store's sales records
are all here.

29:02.640 --> 29:04.280
Officer He, take your time.

29:04.360 --> 29:05.640
I'll make you some tea.

29:05.720 --> 29:07.160
-Thank you.
-No problem.

29:12.160 --> 29:13.560
SALES LOG

29:15.640 --> 29:19.280
SUBJECT SEARCH: SUN ZHENGYONG

29:23.000 --> 29:24.160
DRY CLEANING GIFTCARD REFUND
FOR A SAME DRESS

29:30.480 --> 29:32.840
SUBJECT SEARCH: XU MENG

29:32.920 --> 29:34.360
DRY CLEANING LOG
CLIENT: XU MENG, BUYER: YAO XINCHENG

29:34.440 --> 29:35.280
Found it.

29:35.360 --> 29:39.240
According to the dry-cleaning record,
the buyer linked to this dress

29:39.320 --> 29:40.520
is Yao Xingcheng.

29:40.600 --> 29:44.360
He bought it on December 29, 1996,
at our store.

29:44.440 --> 29:46.600
Yao Xingcheng?

29:46.680 --> 29:47.600
BUYER YAO XINCHENG

29:47.680 --> 29:50.760
RETURN REASON: OTHER REASONS

29:50.840 --> 29:52.400
RETURN DATE: 1997/7/2

29:52.480 --> 29:53.600
That's strange.

29:54.280 --> 29:55.120
What is it?

29:55.720 --> 30:00.280
This Yao Xingcheng's information
only appears in the return record.

30:00.360 --> 30:03.040
His name isn't in the purchase record.

30:03.640 --> 30:07.520
He bought the dress
on December 29 in store.

30:07.600 --> 30:09.760
It was returned on July 2.

30:10.360 --> 30:11.960
The note says, "new returned for old".

30:13.280 --> 30:14.920
What does that mean?

30:15.840 --> 30:18.000
One moment. I'll ask the manager.

30:26.960 --> 30:27.880
Hello, Officer.

30:28.400 --> 30:29.640
I wrote that note.

30:29.720 --> 30:31.720
Back then, this customer
came back after over six months

30:31.800 --> 30:33.240
to make the return.

30:33.320 --> 30:35.600
But the tags and packaging
were all intact.

30:35.680 --> 30:37.800
So the counter canceled the order.

30:38.560 --> 30:40.360
What did the person
who returned it look like?

30:40.440 --> 30:41.840
Do you remember?

30:41.920 --> 30:42.960
I didn't handle the return.

30:43.040 --> 30:46.040
I only found the order while making
that day's report.

30:46.120 --> 30:49.240
This dress had its
button supplier changed in 1997.

30:49.320 --> 30:52.400
This customer bought the old version,
but returned the new one.

30:53.000 --> 30:54.080
I found it strange too.

30:54.160 --> 30:57.000
That's why I wrote that note.

30:58.560 --> 31:00.120
BOWLS FLAGSHIP STORE, SOLD BY SUSAN
COMMENT: WITH ONE DRY CLEANING GIFT CARD

31:00.800 --> 31:02.400
Officer.

31:02.480 --> 31:05.280
The returned dress wasn't bought here.

31:05.360 --> 31:06.640
It was bought
at the provincial flagship store.

31:07.840 --> 31:08.800
What do you mean?

31:09.600 --> 31:10.880
Here's the thing.

31:10.960 --> 31:14.880
This new dress was only distributed
on June 30, 1997.

31:14.960 --> 31:17.400
It arrived at the provincial store
on July 1.

31:17.480 --> 31:19.960
Our Weiyang store is farther away.
It arrived a week later.

31:20.480 --> 31:21.800
So you mean

31:21.880 --> 31:25.360
on July 2, your store wasn't selling
this new style yet?

31:25.440 --> 31:26.480
Right. Look.

31:26.560 --> 31:29.040
On July 2, at 10:05 a.m.,

31:29.120 --> 31:31.520
the provincial flagship store
had a sales record

31:31.600 --> 31:32.440
for the same dress.

31:32.520 --> 31:35.000
But in this record,
there's no customer name.

31:35.080 --> 31:37.600
The return at our store

31:38.320 --> 31:40.200
was at 4:20 p.m. that same day.

31:44.280 --> 31:45.520
Strange.

31:45.600 --> 31:47.160
Bought it in the provincial capital
that morning,

31:47.240 --> 31:48.680
then spent hours rushing to Weiyang,

31:48.760 --> 31:50.160
just to return the dress.

31:50.240 --> 31:51.760
Why go through all that?

31:57.800 --> 31:59.480
This return is strange.

31:59.560 --> 32:01.560
Jessica. Mark it clearly.

32:01.640 --> 32:04.280
In case the customer asks later,
we'll have an explanation.

32:04.360 --> 32:05.640
Yes, Manager.

32:10.640 --> 32:13.320
NOTE: NEW FOR OLD, BOUGHT IN CAPITAL
RETURNED IN WEIYANG. JESSICA

32:15.520 --> 32:18.560
This customer
bought it in the capital that morning,

32:18.640 --> 32:20.000
then returned it in Weiyang
that afternoon.

32:20.080 --> 32:22.040
And it canceled a record
from over six months ago.

32:22.840 --> 32:23.760
Why?

32:26.560 --> 32:28.520
Maybe they wanted to use the return

32:28.600 --> 32:30.960
to erase Yao Xingcheng's purchase record.

32:31.680 --> 32:35.080
Ma'am, can you help me contact
the Jessica who wrote this note?

32:35.160 --> 32:37.080
Jessica from the Weiyang store.

32:37.640 --> 32:39.800
I need to check HR's computer.

32:39.880 --> 32:40.880
One moment.

32:40.960 --> 32:42.640
-Thank you.
-No problem.

32:44.400 --> 32:47.120
Right. Can I make a copy of these files?

32:47.680 --> 32:49.400
Sure. You can copy them yourself.

33:06.560 --> 33:07.520
Uncle Ran,

33:09.640 --> 33:10.600
back then,

33:11.400 --> 33:12.720
did you find this too?

33:19.000 --> 33:20.680
SUBJECT SEARCH: RAN FANGXU

33:22.000 --> 33:23.200
SEARCH

33:23.280 --> 33:25.280
DATE: 2003/1/29, WEIYANG FLAGSHIP
CLIENT: RAN FANGXU

33:27.160 --> 33:28.760
SALESPERSON: JESSICA

33:30.960 --> 33:32.360
STORE: WEIYANG FLAGSHIP
CUSTOMER: RAN FANGXU

33:32.440 --> 33:33.280
Thank you for your cooperation.

33:34.120 --> 33:34.960
Of course.

33:35.040 --> 33:36.680
-I'll get going.
-Okay. Take care.

33:36.760 --> 33:37.640
See him out.

33:38.320 --> 33:39.480
Officer.

33:39.560 --> 33:40.680
New Year is coming soon.

33:40.760 --> 33:43.240
Would you like to see some clothes
and pick one for your family?

33:52.400 --> 33:53.440
Officer.

33:53.520 --> 33:55.520
You're handsome, and you have great taste.

33:55.600 --> 33:57.240
This just came in.
It's the Year of the Goat style.

33:57.320 --> 33:59.360
I can give you an extra discount.

34:10.159 --> 34:11.120
I recovered one file.

34:19.600 --> 34:20.440
Uncle He,

34:21.199 --> 34:23.520
why did Officer Ran save this?

34:24.440 --> 34:25.760
Just close it first.

34:26.639 --> 34:28.120
Right. Eyes off.

34:38.679 --> 34:39.600
He,

34:42.840 --> 34:45.199
this hard drive was probably found
at Wu Shanlong's home.

34:45.800 --> 34:47.480
By procedure, after a case closes,

34:47.560 --> 34:49.639
all assets go to judicial auction.

34:50.400 --> 34:52.000
So this hard drive was wiped.

34:52.600 --> 34:53.600
Looks like

34:54.480 --> 34:57.720
Ran must have bought this hard drive.

34:58.920 --> 35:00.200
I get it.

35:00.280 --> 35:02.000
After this drive was auctioned,

35:02.080 --> 35:05.240
if someone like me knew data recovery,

35:06.720 --> 35:10.160
Officer Ran was afraid the victims
would be hurt again.

35:12.320 --> 35:13.960
That was Ran.

35:15.120 --> 35:17.200
He cared about everyone.

35:21.200 --> 35:23.320
Hello. Please wrap these two for me.

35:24.320 --> 35:26.720
Do you want to wear it now?
I'll take the tag off.

35:27.440 --> 35:28.560
Sure, thanks.

35:32.480 --> 35:35.440
OULI FASHION BOUTIQUE

35:36.040 --> 35:37.120
Welcome.

36:01.680 --> 36:03.240
Do you like this color?

36:06.200 --> 36:08.840
I came to pick a scarf for Sir.

36:08.920 --> 36:09.800
I didn't expect you here.

36:13.960 --> 36:16.480
Which one do you think
would look good on Sir?

36:18.640 --> 36:20.080
No need to bother.

36:20.160 --> 36:22.720
You and Officer He each get one. My treat.

36:23.600 --> 36:24.640
No.

36:24.720 --> 36:26.600
New Year's gift. You can't refuse.

36:32.240 --> 36:33.320
Please wrap them up.

36:33.400 --> 36:34.280
-Sure.
-Thanks.

36:34.360 --> 36:37.760
Sir, I saw your wife
helping you choose for ages.

36:37.840 --> 36:39.880
You two are really close. That's so sweet.

36:52.320 --> 36:53.640
Why did you buy two too?

36:55.200 --> 36:56.760
This one is for Xiaohe.

36:57.400 --> 36:58.800
You got Officer He a gift.

36:58.880 --> 37:01.320
I can't show up empty-handed
and eat for free.

37:16.280 --> 37:18.840
You try it on.

37:20.080 --> 37:21.000
For me?

37:24.080 --> 37:26.440
This, how much was it?

37:26.520 --> 37:28.120
Wool is expensive.

37:29.720 --> 37:31.080
NATIONAL RETAIL PRICE: 1,888 YUAN

37:31.160 --> 37:32.640
This, this is too expensive.

37:32.720 --> 37:34.160
You should return it.

37:35.040 --> 37:35.920
Don't look at the tag price.

37:36.000 --> 37:38.240
I got an extra discount.
It wasn't expensive.

37:40.800 --> 37:41.680
This is a New Year's gift too.

37:41.760 --> 37:42.760
You can't refuse.

37:47.920 --> 37:51.560
You don’t make much every month,
and you still spend like this.

37:52.360 --> 37:53.920
You really don’t know
how to manage your money.

38:08.400 --> 38:10.720
I reached Jessica
from the Weiyang store in 2003.

38:10.800 --> 38:13.000
It matches the clues
Uncle Ran found back then.

38:14.160 --> 38:16.360
We finally caught up with Uncle Ran.

38:16.440 --> 38:19.240
Great. This Yao Xingcheng

38:19.320 --> 38:21.760
is the key to cracking
the Yuanlongli June 30th case.

38:21.840 --> 38:24.360
The Bowls dress at Xu Meng's home
was bought by him.

38:24.960 --> 38:26.320
He didn't want anyone to find out.

38:26.840 --> 38:30.040
So, he used a return
to erase the purchase record.

38:30.640 --> 38:34.560
Also, the man
who went to Mr. Lu to turn red heels

38:34.640 --> 38:36.400
was most likely him too.

38:36.480 --> 38:37.640
Here's the plan.

38:37.720 --> 38:40.440
We keep working both ends.
Once you're back in Weiyang,

38:40.520 --> 38:41.920
go to the bureau first.

38:42.000 --> 38:43.360
Search the internal network.

38:43.440 --> 38:45.880
I'll contact Xu Meng's family now.

38:45.960 --> 38:49.160
We'll try to find this Yao Xingcheng
as soon as possible.

38:49.760 --> 38:51.240
-Okay.
-Talk later.

38:55.080 --> 38:56.880
Auntie Xu.

38:57.680 --> 38:58.920
Xu.

39:00.560 --> 39:01.920
NEW YORK BLOCK

39:02.000 --> 39:05.640
Both corners, put signal blockers on them.

39:05.720 --> 39:08.520
Not one call or text gets out
of this building!

39:08.600 --> 39:10.720
-Got it!
-Okay!

39:15.160 --> 39:16.120
Mr. Qian,

39:16.200 --> 39:19.520
what if the residents run out
and call the police?

39:20.680 --> 39:21.520
Are you stupid?

39:22.560 --> 39:25.240
Cut it off for half an hour,
then turn it back on.

39:25.320 --> 39:28.040
Turn it on, then cut it off.
Cut it off, then turn it on.

39:28.120 --> 39:28.960
AUNTIE XU

39:29.040 --> 39:30.160
Auntie Xu.

39:39.720 --> 39:42.240
NO SERVICE

39:45.720 --> 39:46.840
Qian Dajun!

39:46.920 --> 39:48.800
You shameless piece of trash!

40:02.480 --> 40:03.400
Officer He.

40:04.000 --> 40:05.240
Heading out?

40:05.320 --> 40:06.480
Qian Dajun.

40:08.920 --> 40:11.000
What goes around comes around.

40:11.800 --> 40:14.240
It’s just a matter of time.

40:24.040 --> 40:24.920
See that?

40:25.440 --> 40:28.400
Even that stubborn old man
can't take it anymore.

40:29.240 --> 40:31.240
Those old fools upstairs,

40:31.320 --> 40:33.520
all they’ve got is a big mouth.

40:33.600 --> 40:35.240
Qian Dajun!

40:35.320 --> 40:36.640
You rotten punk!

40:36.720 --> 40:37.960
I'll end you!

40:38.480 --> 40:40.160
Underground garage…

40:42.800 --> 40:45.360
The underground garage
still has a few holdouts.

40:46.120 --> 40:47.880
Especially that Du Mingliang.

40:48.480 --> 40:50.400
Even that little punk dares to act up.

40:50.480 --> 40:51.840
Then we start with him.

40:52.680 --> 40:54.480
Make an example of him.

41:02.960 --> 41:05.400
BLESSING

41:23.800 --> 41:27.360
BLESSING, GOOD FORTUNE

41:40.640 --> 41:41.760
Auntie Xu.

41:43.760 --> 41:44.920
Who is it?

41:50.600 --> 41:52.120
It's me, Auntie Xu.

41:58.680 --> 41:59.880
Officer He?

42:02.520 --> 42:04.960
Officer He, you've gotten old.

42:05.040 --> 42:07.400
Come on, have a seat.
I'll get you some water.

42:07.480 --> 42:08.440
No need.

42:08.960 --> 42:10.440
These are for you.

42:11.080 --> 42:13.000
Thank you.

42:13.080 --> 42:15.640
I'm here to ask about something.

42:16.400 --> 42:19.480
Back then, did Xu Meng and Xu Zhihong

42:19.560 --> 42:23.720
know someone named Yao Xingcheng?

42:24.240 --> 42:25.680
Yao Xingcheng?

42:27.120 --> 42:29.520
Yao Xingcheng.

42:30.440 --> 42:31.280
Yao…

42:32.920 --> 42:35.560
I remember now. I remember.

42:35.640 --> 42:39.400
One year, around New Year,

42:39.480 --> 42:41.360
a young man came by.

42:41.440 --> 42:44.400
He said he was a police officer too.

42:44.480 --> 42:49.120
He asked me about Yao Xingcheng.

42:49.200 --> 42:53.520
But I had never heard that name.

42:55.200 --> 42:59.480
That young man was not only handsome,
but also kind.

43:00.000 --> 43:03.360
When he left, he insisted
on giving me a red envelope.

43:03.440 --> 43:07.440
Officer He, how has he been?

43:08.400 --> 43:09.800
Is he married?

43:09.880 --> 43:11.680
Does he have kids?
